<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/deck/kujo-logomark.svg"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>KUJO / Investor appendix</title><meta name="description" content="Kujo investor diligence: ecosystem responsibilities, recorded execution evidence, technical limitations, and editable financial assumptions."><link rel="canonical" href="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/appendix"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="KUJO / Investor appendix"><meta property="og:description" content="Technical scope, execution artifacts and editable assumptions."><meta property="og:url" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/appendix"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"KUJO / Investor appendix","description":"Technical scope, execution artifacts and editable assumptions.","url":"https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/appendix","inLanguage":"en"}</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/deck/appendix.css"><meta property="og:image" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/social/appendix.4b9459b91a1c.png"><meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/social/appendix.4b9459b91a1c.png"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="KUJO — Investor appendix. Technical scope, execution artifacts and editable assumptions."><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/social/appendix.4b9459b91a1c.png"><meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="KUJO — Investor appendix. Technical scope, execution artifacts and editable assumptions."></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to diligence content</a><header><a href="/">← Return to the presentation</a><p class="eyebrow">KUJO / INVESTOR DILIGENCE / NOVEMBER 2026</p><h1>The evidence behind the argument.</h1><p>Technical scope, execution artifacts and editable assumptions.</p><nav aria-label="Appendix sections"><a href="#architecture">Architecture</a><a href="#maturity">Maturity</a><a href="#evidence">Run evidence</a><a href="#benchmarks">Benchmarks</a><a href="#competition">Competition</a><a href="#market">Market</a><a href="#commercial">Pricing</a><a href="#funding">Funding</a><a href="#budget">Budget</a><a href="#roadmap">Roadmap</a><a href="#risks">Risks</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav></header><main id="main"><section id="architecture"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 01</span><h2>One ecosystem. Separate responsibilities.</h2><p>The architecture below is a composition map. Solid associations describe documented responsibilities; the hosted operating layer is proposed. No automatic universal integration or policy enforcement is claimed.</p><div class="architecture"><details open><summary>Clarity: intent and outcome</summary><p>Kujo compiler/runtime runs programs. Spec defines task contracts. Eval executes configured checks. Language capability policies do not replace container or operating-system boundaries.</p></details><details><summary>Context: inputs and records</summary><p>MCP exposes configured tools/resources. CaseFile captures commands and logs. RunLedger stores supplied results and Git context. Watchdog records supported telemetry and estimated costs.</p></details><details><summary>Control: state and execution</summary><p>Dispatch persists workflow state and approvals. Workcell applies supported host/container limits. ShipCheck checks release-readiness signals. Human reviewers retain authority.</p></details><details><summary>Proposed commercial layer</summary><p>Hosted execution, evidence retention, team review and organization governance. Product integration, multi-tenant isolation, service operations and commercial validation remain work to fund.</p></details></div></section><section id="maturity"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 02</span><h2>Capability and maturity matrix</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scrollable data table"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Capability / maturity</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/kujo/blob/7a13207019a51e61d3db448bc13f59d5b0e332e5/README.md">kujo</a><br><small>T01</small></th><td>VM-first bytecode runtime, compiler and CLI<br><small>1.9.0 release documented</small></td><td>No complete language safety or live-provider certification claim.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/dispatch/blob/18b5c737a73904ae942f0bd1c3baa1f77c2bfb40/README.md">dispatch</a><br><small>T02</small></th><td>Persisted workflow state, approval gates, retries and recovery<br><small>1.4.1 release documented</small></td><td>Trusted local host; effect assurance beta and participant interoperability alpha are experimental.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/workcell/blob/189d7ab6e975301a0e5100b65e8ad3fe4a584573/README.md">workcell</a><br><small>T03</small></th><td>Disposable Git workspace, Docker/Podman resource bounds, declared exports, receipt verification<br><small>1.3.0 stable local contract documented</small></td><td>Requires pinned runtime and supported host; no compromised-host protection. Remote adapters alpha, not certified here.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/eval/blob/c1b263a10702c2fa8ab61ed507029a6bfec2e03d/README.md">eval</a><br><small>T04</small></th><td>Deterministic checks and machine-readable evaluation results<br><small>source inspected; local demo separately verified</small></td><td>Only configured checks; no proof of semantic correctness or independent attestation.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/spec/blob/36da0d7216587809e32dedb91dee3cf4b9e50af1/README.md">spec</a><br><small>T05</small></th><td>Task contracts and acceptance criteria<br><small>1.0.2 release documented</small></td><td>A contract does not enforce all runtime boundaries.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/runledger/blob/ab0ec5d2edb7ffd913f48d092aa6fc17cab58d13/README.md">runledger</a><br><small>T06</small></th><td>Local JSON run receipts, supplied commands/results and Git facts<br><small>1.2.1 release documented</small></td><td>Does not execute or independently prove recorded tests.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/shipcheck/blob/7eedd9e02d8730d65e06e16f4984d909d23539bc/README.md">shipcheck</a><br><small>T07</small></th><td>Explicit release-readiness scans and CI gates<br><small>1.0.2 production-forward alpha</small></td><td>Not release certification; a human decides to ship.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/casefile/blob/92e1d9bee2faaba322476e82dcea7510850885e0/README.md">casefile</a><br><small>T08</small></th><td>Capture executed command output and exit code into debugging bundles<br><small>1.0.2 documented; demo locally verified</small></td><td>Trusted local host, bounded/redacted logs; successful capture can contain failed command.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/watchdog/blob/7a0bd9a63d68421831ed66d6eed29805c48e1b24/README.md">watchdog</a><br><small>T09</small></th><td>OpenAI-compatible proxy and local telemetry database/dashboard<br><small>1.2.2 release documented</small></td><td>Estimated costs are not invoices. Authentication/TLS/retention are deployment responsibilities.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/kennel/blob/6e2fc20560037970df5202e1b1ca8f61c3395570/README.md">kennel</a><br><small>T10</small></th><td>Kujo package manifests, resolution and installation<br><small>source inspected</small></td><td>Package distribution is not adoption evidence.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/mcp/blob/77180a3a6c104f0c5b185cefa1f6d0835edb704b/README.md">mcp</a><br><small>T11</small></th><td>Kujo MCP server framework and guarded repo scaffolding<br><small>1.3.3 release documented</small></td><td>Remote deployments need ingress/auth/capacity review; not blanket agent integration.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/README.md">packwrite</a><br><small>T12</small></th><td>Compiles prompt/context into validated agent execution packs<br><small>1.1.1 installed</small></td><td>Does not implement the project. Provider availability depends on credentials/model.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/kujo-workflows/blob/d766eae4fd9a131e51c34796d029fd3bc6974689/README.md">kujo-workflows</a><br><small>T13</small></th><td>Portable bounded execution/evaluation workflow harness<br><small>source inspected; task gates run locally</small></td><td>Bash harness records/gates actions; editorial judgment is performed by this assistant, not a built-in investor judge.</td></tr><tr><th><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/presentations/blob/879211bbf3707ec1ec6a9e19bb9ce2b1f9691bfa/README.md">presentations</a><br><small>T14</small></th><td>Kujo SSG/SiteKit static deck rendering, notes console, print/read editions<br><small>0.3.1 preview; built locally</small></td><td>Preview APIs may change; fixed 16:9 canvas needs reading edition on small screens.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id="evidence"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 03</span><h2>Inspect the recorded run</h2><p><strong>Authentic local execution; deliberately seeded fixture.</strong> The assistant authored a small coding task, recorded its failure, corrected the formula and ran the checks. This is not a customer incident, live production agent run or independent attestation.</p><div class="evidence-nav"><button data-evidence="request">Request</button><button data-evidence="diff">Code change</button><button data-evidence="before">Failed command</button><button data-evidence="after">Passed command</button><button data-evidence="eval">Evaluation</button><button data-evidence="decision">Decision</button></div><pre id="evidence-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Selected execution artifact">Select an artifact to inspect it.</pre><p>CaseFile captures command exit status and bounded output. Eval checks the explicit conditions. Files are trusted-local artifacts; SHA-256 detects changes relative to this manifest, not host compromise.</p><details><summary>All original artifacts and reproduction files</summary><div class="file-list"><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/DECISION.md">DECISION.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/REQUEST.md">REQUEST.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/case.json">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/case.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/case.md">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/case.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/combined.log">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/combined.log</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/command.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/command.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/environment.json">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/environment.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/git-diff-stat.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/git-diff-stat.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/git-recent-commits.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/git-recent-commits.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/git-status.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/git-status.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/handoff.md">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/handoff.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/reproduction.md">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/reproduction.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/stderr.log">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/stderr.log</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/stdout.log">casefile/2026-11-09-091944-before/stdout.log</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/case.json">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/case.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/case.md">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/case.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/combined.log">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/combined.log</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/command.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/command.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/environment.json">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/environment.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/git-diff-stat.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/git-diff-stat.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/git-recent-commits.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/git-recent-commits.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/git-status.txt">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/git-status.txt</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/handoff.md">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/handoff.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/reproduction.md">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/reproduction.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/stderr.log">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/stderr.log</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/stdout.log">casefile/2026-11-09-091948-after/stdout.log</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/change.patch">change.patch</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/commands.json">commands.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/environment.json">environment.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/artifact-manifest.json">eval-results/artifact-manifest.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/badge.json">eval-results/badge.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/cli-summary.json">eval-results/cli-summary.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/eval-report.md">eval-results/eval-report.md</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/eval-report.md.cache.json">eval-results/eval-report.md.cache.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/evaluation-result.json">eval-results/evaluation-result.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/history.json">eval-results/history.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/last_failures.json">eval-results/last_failures.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/last_run.json">eval-results/last_run.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval-results/summary.json">eval-results/summary.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/eval.json">eval.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/manifest.json">manifest.json</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/ownership.mjs">ownership.mjs</a><a href="/assets/deck/evidence/test.mjs">test.mjs</a></div></details></section><section id="benchmarks"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 04</span><h2>A correctness fixture, not a performance claim</h2><p>Method: Node assertions check 6/30 = 20% and 3/30 = 10%; the initial denominator intentionally adds the raise and fails. CaseFile captures both executions. Eval runs the assertion command and checks the corrected source expression. Observed result: two configured Eval checks passed, with the earlier assertion failure retained.</p><p>Reproduce with <code>python3 scripts/record-demo.py</code> from the source deck, using the sibling CaseFile, Eval and Kujo 1.9.0 checkout. This overwrites the recorded fixture artifacts; retain the original before comparing runs. Timings are recorded but not a statistically meaningful benchmark. No competitor benchmark, latency advantage, comprehensive correctness or security certification is claimed.</p><p>Future benchmark plan: publish fixed repositories, pinned environments, task corpus, failure taxonomy, complete attempts, repeated seeds and independent reproduction. Measure reviewer time, evidence completeness and failure recovery alongside task success.</p></section><section id="competition"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 05</span><h2>Strong alternatives define the bar</h2><p>Representative comparison, source/documentation review dated 2026-11-09, not hands-on parity testing. <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/copilot-surfaces/copilot-on-github">GitHub Copilot</a> and <a href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence">LangGraph</a> already offer substantial capability. Observability systems such as <a href="https://opentelemetry.io/docs/">OpenTelemetry</a> standardize telemetry; CI systems such as <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/actions">GitHub Actions</a> execute workflow checks. Kujo should complement or replace specific responsibilities only after evidence.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scrollable data table"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Coding agents / existing CI</th><th>Orchestration frameworks</th><th>Kujo documented scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Execution boundaries</td><td>Existing agent environment controls; inspect configuration</td><td>Application/host responsibility</td><td>Workcell documented OCI bounds</td></tr><tr><td>Evidence provenance</td><td>Repository/session history</td><td>Checkpointed state and traces</td><td>CaseFile command bundles; RunLedger supplied receipts</td></tr><tr><td>Reproducibility</td><td>Depends on task, dependencies and environment</td><td>Requires deterministic/idempotent design</td><td>Pinned fixtures and exported artifacts; host trust remains</td></tr><tr><td>Recovery</td><td>Product/workflow specific</td><td>Checkpoint recovery documented</td><td>Dispatch persisted state; Workcell scoped recovery</td></tr><tr><td>Policy enforcement</td><td>Organization and agent settings</td><td>Application-defined controls</td><td>Specific tool contracts, not universal language enforcement</td></tr><tr><td>Release verification</td><td>Git review and CI ecosystem</td><td>Application-defined</td><td>Eval + ShipCheck checks; human decision</td></tr><tr><td>Integration depth</td><td>Strong existing developer distribution</td><td>Broad agent application ecosystem</td><td>Native language/tooling cohesion; hosted layer proposed</td></tr><tr><td>Language support</td><td>Existing repositories</td><td>Python/JS ecosystems</td><td>Kujo tooling can inspect non-Kujo application code</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Potential defensibility: stable evidence contracts, integration quality, reproducible operations and retained developer use. These are future advantages to earn. Open interfaces reduce lock-in and ease adoption; no exclusive technology moat is asserted.</p></section><section id="market"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 06</span><h2>Edit the bottom-up assumptions</h2><p>All counts and contract values are unvalidated planning assumptions. The model estimates a narrow organization-level service opportunity, not the entire AI industry.</p><div class="inputs"><label>Initial organizations<input id="organizations" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="2000"></label><label>Annual contract, USD<input id="acv" type="number" min="0" max="10000000" value="24000"></label><label>Attainable customers<input id="customers" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="100"></label></div><output id="market-output" aria-live="polite"></output><p>Expansion scenario: 10,000 organizations × $60K = $600M annual pool. This is a separate, longer-term hypothesis, not additive TAM. Validate organization counts, budget ownership, competition, retention and willingness to pay.</p></section><section id="commercial"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 07</span><h2>Proposed pricing needs customer evidence</h2><div class="columns"><div><h3>Developer</h3><p>Open local tooling. Adoption measured by successful and repeated evidence runs.</p></div><div><h3>Team: $24K / year</h3><p>Hypothesis for hosted retention, shared review and team controls. Execution usage may be separate.</p></div><div><h3>Enterprise: $60K / year</h3><p>Hypothesis for governance, deployment support and organization controls. No validated pricing or contracts.</p></div></div><p>Commercial validation sequence: instrument active repositories → investigate repeated use → recruit design partners → paid pilots → retention and expansion. Infrastructure cost, support load and gross margin require actual usage data.</p></section><section id="funding"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 08</span><h2>Funding scenarios and dilution</h2><p>Working scenario: $6M at $30M post-money. These are planning inputs, not agreed terms or validated valuation. Simplified ownership = raise ÷ post-money; SAFE mechanics, option pools and other instruments can change outcomes.</p><div class="inputs"><label>Raise<select id="raise"><option value="3000000">$3M</option><option value="6000000" selected>$6M</option><option value="8000000">$8M</option><option value="10000000">$10M</option></select></label><label>Post-money USD<input id="postmoney" type="number" min="1000000" max="1000000000" value="30000000"></label><label>Runway months<input id="months" type="number" min="1" max="120" value="24"></label></div><output id="funding-output" aria-live="polite"></output><div id="budget" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scenario allocation table"></div><button id="export">Export current assumptions JSON</button><p>At fixed $30M post-money: $3M → 10%; $6M → 20%; $8M → 26.67%; $10M → 33.33%. A later round that dilutes all holders by 20% reduces a 20% holding to 16%.</p><p>$3M prioritizes one flagship workflow and a smaller team. $6M supports parallel runtime, execution and developer experience work. $8M/$10M permit more integration and commercial capacity, conditional on evidence of demand.</p></section><section id="budget"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 09</span><h2>Twenty-four-month operating plan</h2><p>$6M case: $3.30M engineering; $600K infrastructure; $600K distribution; $600K operations; $900K reserve. Non-reserve operating average: $212,500/month. Gross capital divided by 24 months: $250,000/month, including reserve.</p><p>Founder base: $150K/year, or $300K over two years. Illustrative 25% payroll burden makes $375K, included in engineering. Remaining engineering: $2.925M; at $240K per engineer-year, approximately 12.19 engineer-years. Location and hiring ramp materially affect this model.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scrollable data table"><table><thead><tr><th>Quarter</th><th>Operating spend</th><th>Cumulative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Q1</td><td>$350,000</td><td>$350,000</td></tr><tr><td>Q2</td><td>$450,000</td><td>$800,000</td></tr><tr><td>Q3</td><td>$550,000</td><td>$1,350,000</td></tr><tr><td>Q4</td><td>$650,000</td><td>$2,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Q5</td><td>$700,000</td><td>$2,700,000</td></tr><tr><td>Q6</td><td>$750,000</td><td>$3,450,000</td></tr><tr><td>Q7</td><td>$800,000</td><td>$4,250,000</td></tr><tr><td>Q8</td><td>$850,000</td><td>$5,100,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Reserve stays $900K. No revenue offset assumed. This simplified allocation is not a monthly cash-flow forecast. Benefits, taxes, legal, security and customer support must be priced before commitments.</p></section><section id="roadmap"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 10</span><h2>Hire against measurable milestones</h2><ol class="roadmap"><li><h3>Months 0–6</h3><p>Hire execution reliability and developer experience engineers; harden one flagship evidence workflow. Publish reproducible benchmark protocol and recruit external reviewers. Proposed target: 10 independently activated teams.</p></li><li><h3>Months 6–12</h3><p>Expand runtime/integration capacity after activation evidence. Proposed targets: 5 design partners, 3 paid pilots and measured four-week retention. Publish all benchmark limitations.</p></li><li><h3>Months 12–24</h3><p>Add customer engineering when support demand is demonstrated. Test repeatable acquisition, renewal and expansion. 100 customers at $24K is a scenario to test, not a committed forecast.</p></li></ol><p>December 2026 campaign is planned. Measure unique activated repositories, successful evidence runs, repeat usage, qualified conversations and paid conversions by cohort. Partnerships are prospective.</p></section><section id="risks"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 11</span><h2>Technical ambition must survive commercial reality</h2><dl><dt>Language adoption</dt><dd>New language adoption may take years. Sell useful workflow infrastructure independently of migration.</dd><dt>Integration complexity</dt><dd>Tools have distinct contracts and runtime pins. Fund one reliable flagship experience before promising seamless coverage.</dd><dt>Trust and security</dt><dd>Editable local evidence is not independent attestation. Hosted custody, tenant isolation and retention need dedicated design and review.</dd><dt>Incumbents</dt><dd>Agents, CI and observability vendors can expand into accountability. Prove lower operational burden and repeat use.</dd><dt>Demand and pricing</dt><dd>No verified customer, retention or revenue data supplied. Validate the beachhead and pricing through actual pilots.</dd><dt>Founder concentration</dt><dd>Broaden maintainership, documentation and release ownership. Confirm contributor attribution and biography before distribution.</dd></dl></section><section id="sources"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / 12</span><h2>Source register and investor follow-up</h2><p>Research cut: 2026-11-09. Release inventory dated 2026-10-22 is not a blanket current-HEAD guarantee. Full claim register is retained in source at research/CLAIMS.md.</p><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/kujo/blob/7a13207019a51e61d3db448bc13f59d5b0e332e5/README.md">T01 / kujo / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/dispatch/blob/18b5c737a73904ae942f0bd1c3baa1f77c2bfb40/README.md">T02 / dispatch / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/workcell/blob/189d7ab6e975301a0e5100b65e8ad3fe4a584573/README.md">T03 / workcell / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/eval/blob/c1b263a10702c2fa8ab61ed507029a6bfec2e03d/README.md">T04 / eval / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/spec/blob/36da0d7216587809e32dedb91dee3cf4b9e50af1/README.md">T05 / spec / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/runledger/blob/ab0ec5d2edb7ffd913f48d092aa6fc17cab58d13/README.md">T06 / runledger / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/shipcheck/blob/7eedd9e02d8730d65e06e16f4984d909d23539bc/README.md">T07 / shipcheck / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/casefile/blob/92e1d9bee2faaba322476e82dcea7510850885e0/README.md">T08 / casefile / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/watchdog/blob/7a0bd9a63d68421831ed66d6eed29805c48e1b24/README.md">T09 / watchdog / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/kennel/blob/6e2fc20560037970df5202e1b1ca8f61c3395570/README.md">T10 / kennel / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/mcp/blob/77180a3a6c104f0c5b185cefa1f6d0835edb704b/README.md">T11 / mcp / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/README.md">T12 / packwrite / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/kujo-workflows/blob/d766eae4fd9a131e51c34796d029fd3bc6974689/README.md">T13 / kujo-workflows / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/kujolang/presentations/blob/879211bbf3707ec1ec6a9e19bb9ce2b1f9691bfa/README.md">T14 / presentations / pinned source</a></li><li><a href="https://survey.stackoverflow.co/2026/ai">M03/M04: Stack Overflow 2026 AI survey</a></li><li><a href="https://robertdevore.com/about/">F01: Robert DeVore public biography</a></li><li><a href="https://docs.kujolang.ai/ecosystem/releases/">Release inventory</a></li><li><a href="https://kujolang.ai">Kujo official site</a></li></ul><p>Before investor distribution: supply verified adoption and commercial metrics, confirm founder attribution and contact details, validate pricing/budget assumptions, and obtain financing advice on actual instrument terms. No current customer or investor commitment is represented.</p><a href="https://robertdevore.com/contact/">Investor contact ↗</a></section></main><footer>KUJO · Trust at the speed of AI. · Planning assumptions are not commitments.</footer><script src="/assets/deck/appendix.js" defer></script><script type="module" src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/vce701823e78c4301a35b7e07294d87301792088814092" integrity="sha512-UKNk8GbxkABxKcXYuLkO16EleLGUkcvJWtpSNmExE0Too3ZaFAxTscNWEc1OdAv5/BikHawapSCaiD2XCmp+Bw==" data-cf-beacon='{"version":"2024.11.0","token":"1d30a17a0e01472db240809ad42c0b1f","r":1,"spa":2}' crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
